      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Given the head of a linked list, remove the nth node from \nthe end of the list and return its head.\n\nWHAT TO DO : \n1. Find the middle element , it can work , if we can search in two \nseparate lists",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Given the head of a linked list, remove the nth node from \nthe end of the list and return its head.\n\nWHAT TO DO : \n1. Find the middle element , it can work , if we can search in two \nseparate lists",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
